# TX-08 / old AI-13 — DRAFT ONLY. Not applied to /Makefile (owner decision: any workflow change).
# Choice (c): a local make gate the owner runs before every export, read-only on the warehouse
# that is about to be exported (data/dev.duckdb). Why, in PROVENANCE.txt ("AI-13 CHOICE").
#
# Proposed change to /Makefile, section "##   Data export":
#
#   1. a new target real-data-gate (read-only: `dbt test` selects, it never writes a model;
#      the two python checks only read);
#   2. app-data and app-data-check depend on it, so an export cannot run on a build whose
#      full-data tests are red. app-data-canary stays ungated (fast local loop, never published).
#   3. An escape hatch is NOT added on purpose: skipping the gate means calling
#      scripts/export_app_data.py directly, which is visible in the shell history.
#
# --- patch (unified, against Makefile lines 251-259 of 2026-11-08) ---------------------------
#
# ##   Data export
#-app-data:  ## Export warehouse → app/public/data/ parquet + _manifest.json
#+real-data-gate:  ## Real-data gate (TX-08/AI-13): every dbt test at full-data thresholds + fct_* oracle + data profile, read-only on data/dev.duckdb
#+	cd transform && ../.venv/bin/dbt test --profiles-dir profiles --target dev
#+	cd transform && ../.venv/bin/python scripts/snapshot_model_hashes.py --check --db ../data/dev.duckdb
#+	./.venv/bin/python transform/scripts/snapshot_data_profile.py --db data/dev.duckdb --check
#+
#+app-data: real-data-gate  ## Export warehouse → app/public/data/ parquet + _manifest.json (after real-data-gate)
# 	./.venv/bin/python scripts/export_app_data.py
#
# app-data-canary:  ## Export canary tables only (fast)
# 	./.venv/bin/python scripts/export_app_data.py --canary
#
#-app-data-check:  ## CI drift gate: regenerate manifest and diff (no write)
#+app-data-check: real-data-gate  ## CI drift gate: regenerate manifest and diff (no write)
# 	./.venv/bin/python scripts/export_app_data.py --check
#
# and add real-data-gate to the .PHONY list at the top.
#
# Caveats the owner should know before applying:
#   - the hash and profile baselines are re-taken once after TX-01..07 land (TX-07 note); until
#     then the second and third lines report the known TX-01..07 drift and the gate is red for that
#     reason alone. Apply this after the re-take.
#   - `dbt test` on dev runs ~1,100 tests at 1 dbt thread as configured in profiles (dev: threads 4);
#     measured on the scratch copy in PROVENANCE.txt.
#
# --- optional (a): the same gate as a workflow on the self-hosted runner -----------------------
# Not recommended now (no runner is configured: pipeline.yml is guarded by vars.PIPELINE_ENABLED
# and vars.PIPELINE_RUNNER). If the owner later configures the runner, this job is the read-only
# shape: it never builds, it tests the reviewed build already on the runner's disk.
